  {
    "id" : "file-length-limit",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Complexity",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce File Length Limit",
    "description" : "This rule enforces a maximum number of lines per file to improve maintainability and reduce complexity.",
    "explanation" : "## file-length-limit\n\n_Description_: This rule enforces a maximum number of lines per file, in order to aid in maintainability and reduce complexity.\n\n_Configuration_:\n\n- `max`: (int) a maximum number of lines in a file. Must be non-negative integers. 0 means the rule is disabled (default `0`);\n- `skipComments` (`skipcomments`, `skip-comments`): (bool) if true ignore and do not count lines containing just comments (default `false`);\n- `skipBlankLines` (`skipblanklines`, `skip-blank-lines`): (bool) if true ignore and do not count lines made up purely of whitespace (default `false`).\n\nExamples:\n\n```toml\n[rule.file-length-limit]\narguments = [{ max = 100, skipComments = true, skipBlankLines = true }]\n```\n\n```toml\n[rule.file-length-limit]\narguments = [{ max = 100, skip-comments = true, skip-blank-lines = true }]\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "filename-format",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Filename Format",
    "description" : "Enforces conventions on source file names to match a specified regular expression pattern, by default allowing filenames matching ^[_A-Za-z0-9][_A-Za-z0-9-]*\\.go$",
    "explanation" : "## filename-format\n\n_Description_: enforces conventions on source file names. By default, the rule enforces filenames of the form `^[_A-Za-z0-9][_A-Za-z0-9-]*\\.go$`.\nOptionally, the rule can be configured to enforce other forms.\n\n_Configuration_: (string) regular expression for source filenames.\n\nExample:\n\n```toml\n[rule.filename-format]\narguments = [\"^[_a-z][_a-z0-9]*\\\\.go$\"]\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "flag-parameter",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Flag Parameters",
    "description" : "Detects boolean parameters that create control coupling between functions, where one function controls the behavior of another by passing information on what to do.",
    "explanation" : "## flag-parameter\n\n_Description_: If a function controls the flow of another by passing it information on what to do, both functions are said to be [control-coupled](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coupling_(computer_programming)#Procedural_programming).\nCoupling among functions must be minimized for better maintainability of the code.\nThis rule warns on boolean parameters that create a control coupling.\n\n_Configuration_: N/A",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
