    "category" : "Complexity",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Function Length Limits",
    "description" : "This rule enforces limits on the length of functions by restricting the number of statements and/or lines they contain to improve readability and maintainability.",
    "explanation" : "## function-length\n\n_Description_: Functions too long (with many statements and/or lines) can be hard to understand.\n\n_Configuration_: (int,int) the maximum allowed statements and lines. Must be non-negative integers. Set to 0 to disable the check\n\nExample:\n\n```toml\n[rule.function-length]\narguments = [10, 0]\n```\n\nWill check for functions exceeding 10 statements and will not check the number of lines of functions",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 15,
