  {
    "id" : "range-val-in-closure",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid range variable reuse in closure",
    "description" : "Detects when a range variable in a loop is used inside a closure, which can lead to unexpected values being captured by goroutines or closures.",
    "explanation" : "## range-val-in-closure\n\n_Description_: Range variables in a loop are reused at each iteration; therefore a goroutine created in a loop will point to the range variable\nwith from the upper scope. This way, the goroutine could use the variable with an undesired value.\nThis rule warns when a range value (or index) is used inside a closure.\n\n_Configuration_: N/A\n\n_Note_: This rule is irrelevant for Go 1.22+.",
    "enabled" : false,
