    "id" : "unhandled-error",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Explicit Handling of Returned Errors",
    "description" : "This rule warns when errors returned by a function are not explicitly handled by the caller.",
    "explanation" : "## unhandled-error\n\n_Description_: This rule warns when errors returned by a function are not explicitly handled on the caller side.\n\n_Configuration_: function names regexp patterns to ignore\n\nExample:\n\n```toml\n[rule.unhandled-error]\narguments = [\n  '^os\\.(CreateTemp|WriteFile|Chmod)$',\n  '^fmt\\.Print',\n  'myFunction',\n  '^net\\.',\n  '^(bytes\\.Buffer|string\\.Writer)\\.Write(Byte|Rune|String)?$',\n]\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
