    "id" : "use-fmt-print",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce use of fmt.Print instead of built-in print/println",
    "description" : "This rule enforces replacing calls to the built-in print and println functions with their equivalents from the fmt standard package in Go.",
    "explanation" : "## use-fmt-print\n\n_Description_: This rule proposes to replace calls to built-in `print` and `println` with their equivalents from `fmt` standard package.\n\n`print` and `println` built-in functions are not recommended for use-cases other than\n[language boostraping and are not guaranteed to stay in the language](https://go.dev/ref/spec#Bootstrapping).\n\n_Configuration_: N/A",
